WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.288 --> 00:00:15.988
what do we do?"

2
00:00:16.328 --> 00:00:18.789
Cole asked, staring after the mystery man.

3
00:00:18.809 --> 00:00:20.769
"Do you think he's the culprit?"

4
00:00:21.690 --> 00:00:22.610
Maggie frowned.

5
00:00:23.290 --> 00:00:24.130
"I don't get it.

6
00:00:24.771 --> 00:00:26.091
Nobody here knows him.

7
00:00:26.751 --> 00:00:29.112
Why would some stranger slash our tires?"

8
00:00:30.112 --> 00:00:33.754
"People get robbed by strangers all the time," Cole pointed out.

9
00:00:33.774 --> 00:00:36.575
"That's different," Henry said.

10
00:00:36.595 --> 00:00:38.636
"Robbers have a motive.

11
00:00:39.396 --> 00:00:42.017
They want the money or other stuff that they steal.

12
00:00:43.018 --> 00:00:45.799
What's that guy's motive for slashing our tires?"

13
00:00:46.800 --> 00:00:48.200
"I don't know," Cole said.

14
00:00:48.220 --> 00:00:50.281
"But I think the new tires are here."

15
00:00:51.182 --> 00:00:52.762
A van was pulling into the field.

16
00:00:53.403 --> 00:00:56.004
It had the Belltown Bikes logo painted on the side.

17
00:00:59.176 --> 00:01:04.078
Several of the bike shop's employees jumped out and started helping people replace their tires.

18
00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:09.740
Before long all the bikes were fixed.

19
00:01:11.721 --> 00:01:15.783
Ms. Hernandez made the riders line up so she could make sure everyone was there.

20
00:01:16.663 --> 00:01:17.884
Then she got on her bike.

21
00:01:17.904 --> 00:01:20.325
"Time to get back on the trail!"

22
00:01:20.725 --> 00:01:21.365
she called out.

23
00:01:21.385 --> 00:01:23.986
"Hip, hip, hooray!"

24
00:01:24.466 --> 00:01:26.307
Melanie cheered, jumping up and down.

25
00:01:26.327 --> 00:01:30.660
"Go, Belltown!"

26
00:01:30.680 --> 00:01:32.160
Soon Henry was back on the trail.

27
00:01:32.981 --> 00:01:35.061
But he wasn't paying attention to the scenery.

28
00:01:35.781 --> 00:01:37.702
He was still thinking about the mystery.

29
00:01:37.722 --> 00:01:42.423
"We need to keep working on this case," he told Maggie and Cole.

30
00:01:42.443 --> 00:01:45.124
"Why?" Maggie asked.

31
00:01:45.144 --> 00:01:47.705
"That mystery man probably did it.

32
00:01:48.585 --> 00:01:51.386
Why else would he lie to us about being a newspaper reporter?"

33
00:01:51.406 --> 00:01:53.867
"I don't know," Henry said.

34
00:01:53.887 --> 00:01:56.127
"He might have other reasons."

35
00:01:57.167 --> 00:01:57.828
Cole nodded.

36
00:01:57.848 --> 00:02:00.505
"Yeah. Maybe he's a spy!"

37
00:02:01.405 --> 00:02:02.406
Henry doubted that.

38
00:02:03.026 --> 00:02:06.609
But he had a feeling The Lemonade Detectives were missing an important clue.

39
00:02:06.629 --> 00:02:10.271
"Let's split up and talk to people again," he said.

40
00:02:10.291 --> 00:02:16.535
"If we can prove everybody else didn't do it, we can investigate that mystery man."

41
00:02:20.798 --> 00:02:24.000
They spent the next few minutes talking to people as they rode along.

42
00:02:27.148 --> 00:02:30.550
Henry questioned different riders about what they'd seen during the break.

43
00:02:31.431 --> 00:02:35.374
The more he learned, the more he realized that most riders had alibis.

44
00:02:36.434 --> 00:02:40.537
Either they hadn't left the picnic area, or they'd been with other people when they had.

45
00:02:41.518 --> 00:02:42.879
Then he caught up to William.

46
00:02:42.899 --> 00:02:44.960
"I guess Ms.

47
00:02:44.980 --> 00:02:47.382
Hernandez talked him out of quitting," he thought.

48
00:02:47.402 --> 00:02:51.645
"Hi, William," Henry called.

49
00:02:51.665 --> 00:02:53.166
"Are you having fun?"

50
00:02:54.066 --> 00:02:55.227
William looked over at him.

51
00:02:55.247 --> 00:02:57.413
"Sure, I guess so."

52
00:02:57.433 --> 00:02:59.594
"Good," Henry said.

53
00:02:59.614 --> 00:03:02.156
"Because I heard you talking to Ms.

54
00:03:02.176 --> 00:03:03.177
Hernandez earlier.

55
00:03:04.277 --> 00:03:06.539
Why did you want to quit partway through the ride?"

56
00:03:07.440 --> 00:03:09.501
William looked surprised and then annoyed.

57
00:03:09.521 --> 00:03:12.363
"None of your business," he muttered.

58
00:03:13.324 --> 00:03:15.085
Then he sped up and rode off.

59
00:03:15.785 --> 00:03:18.227
His fancy mountain bike could go really fast.

60
00:03:19.128 --> 00:03:22.690
Henry was wondering whether he should try to catch up when he heard Maggie.

61
00:03:22.710 --> 00:03:25.092
"Henry! Wait up!"

62
00:03:25.788 --> 00:03:28.250
A second later she and Cole both caught up to him.

63
00:03:29.310 --> 00:03:31.351
The three of them discussed what they'd found out.

64
00:03:31.371 --> 00:03:37.034
"It seems like there are only five people who don't have alibis for the time of the crime,"

65
00:03:37.375 --> 00:03:38.035
Henry said.

66
00:03:38.055 --> 00:03:39.976
"Nathan, Ms.

67
00:03:40.016 --> 00:03:43.638
Hernandez, Tina, William, and the mystery man."

68
00:03:43.658 --> 00:03:48.421
"We know Nathan would never slash people's tires," Cole said.

69
00:03:49.361 --> 00:03:50.102
Henry nodded.

70
00:03:50.122 --> 00:03:52.123
"I think we can cross Ms.

71
00:03:52.163 --> 00:03:53.544
Hernandez off the list too.

72
00:03:54.464 --> 00:03:59.068
That leaves three suspects: Tina, William, and the mystery man."

73
00:03:59.088 --> 00:04:02.290
"I still think Tina did it," Cole said.

74
00:04:02.310 --> 00:04:07.614
"Why would she come on the ride to raise money for Belltown High unless she wanted to cause

75
00:04:07.694 --> 00:04:10.917
trouble?" "I don't know," Henry said.

76
00:04:10.937 --> 00:04:13.459
"But we can't assume it was her.

77
00:04:14.420 --> 00:04:17.502
We thought it was Joey, and he had an alibi, remember?"

78
00:04:18.403 --> 00:04:19.944
He rode around a curve in the trail.

79
00:04:20.880 --> 00:04:25.624
He was thinking so hard, it took him a second to spot the rider stopped by the side

80
00:04:25.644 --> 00:04:26.164
of the trail.

81
00:04:27.045 --> 00:04:27.826
It was Nathan.

82
00:04:28.466 --> 00:04:31.108
He was standing beside his bike, looking worried.

83
00:04:31.769 --> 00:04:33.871
The Lemonade Detectives stopped beside him.

84
00:04:33.891 --> 00:04:35.692
"What's wrong?"

85
00:04:36.092 --> 00:04:36.833
Maggie asked.

86
00:04:36.853 --> 00:04:38.554
"It's my bike."

87
00:04:39.295 --> 00:04:40.856
Nathan pointed toward the gears.

88
00:04:40.876 --> 00:04:42.918
"The chain fell off!

89
00:04:43.538 --> 00:04:44.779
And I don't know how to fix it.

90
00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:46.341
Can you guys help?"

91
00:04:47.221 --> 00:04:48.282
Henry shook his head.

92
00:04:48.302 --> 00:04:50.324
"I don't know how to fix it either."

93
00:04:51.276 --> 00:04:52.537
He looked at Maggie and Cole.

94
00:04:52.557 --> 00:04:53.998
"What about you two?"

95
00:04:54.899 --> 00:04:56.040
They shook their heads too.

96
00:04:56.060 --> 00:05:01.604
"Maybe you can leave your bike here and ride double with one of us," Maggie suggested.

97
00:05:02.504 --> 00:05:04.266
Just then Joey rode toward them.

98
00:05:05.026 --> 00:05:06.387
He smirked when he saw them.

99
00:05:07.328 --> 00:05:09.690
"Having bike trouble, Belltown losers?"

100
00:05:10.150 --> 00:05:10.630
he yelled.

101
00:05:10.650 --> 00:05:13.152
"Good, you deserve it!"

102
00:05:14.753 --> 00:05:18.216
He sped around the next curve, making dirt fly at them as he passed.

103
00:05:19.948 --> 00:05:21.910
"Go back to Valley High, you bully!"

104
00:05:22.230 --> 00:05:22.871
Maggie yelled.

105
00:05:22.891 --> 00:05:24.792
"Forget about him."

106
00:05:25.493 --> 00:05:26.313
Nathan sighed.

107
00:05:26.954 --> 00:05:28.695
"What am I going to do about my bike?"

108
00:05:29.836 --> 00:05:31.578
A few more riders rounded the curve.

109
00:05:32.519 --> 00:05:34.761
Some of them looked over at Nathan's broken bike.

110
00:05:35.441 --> 00:05:36.482
But nobody stopped.

111
00:05:39.224 --> 00:05:40.665
Then Tina rode into view.

112
00:05:41.446 --> 00:05:44.389
As soon as she saw Nathan's bike, she steered toward him.

113
00:05:44.409 --> 00:05:48.272
"Your chain fell off, huh?"

114
00:05:48.637 --> 00:05:49.980
she said with a friendly smile.

115
00:05:50.000 --> 00:05:51.123
"Don't worry.

116
00:05:51.143 --> 00:05:53.067
I can help you fix it."
